{"id":"mahabharata-5-101","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":101,"title":"एकाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 101 · Bhogavati and the serpent Sumukha","summary":{"en":"Narada shows Matali Bhogavati, the city of the serpents ruled by Vasuki, and names many great Nagas. Matali sees the handsome young serpent Sumukha, grandson of Aryaka, and chooses him as his daughter's husband.","kn":"ವಾಸುಕಿ ಆಳುವ ನಾಗರ ನಗರ ಭೋಗವತಿಯನ್ನು ನಾರದರು ತೋರಿಸಿ ಅನೇಕ ಮಹಾನಾಗಗಳನ್ನು ಹೆಸರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಆರ್ಯಕನ ಮೊಮ್ಮಗ ಸುಂದರ ಯುವನಾಗ ಸುಮುಖನನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಮಾತಲಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಮಗಳ ಪತಿಯಾಗಿ ಆರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"नारद मातलि को वासुकि द्वारा शासित नागों की नगरी भोगवती दिखाते हैं और अनेक महानागों के नाम बताते हैं। मातलि आर्यक के पौत्र सुन्दर युवा नाग सुमुख को देखकर उसे अपनी पुत्री के पति के रूप में चुनते हैं।","te":"వాసుకి పాలించే నాగుల నగరం భోగవతిని నారదుడు చూపించి అనేక మహానాగులను పేర్కొంటాడు. ఆర్యకుని మనవడు అందమైన యువనాగుడు సుముఖుని చూసి మాతలి అతనిని కుమార్తె భర్తగా ఎంచుకుంటాడు.","ta":"வாஸுகி ஆளும் நாகர்களின் நகரான போகவதியை நாரதர் காட்டிப் பல பெரும் நாகர்களைப் பெயரிடுகிறார். ஆர்யகனின் பேரனான அழகிய இளம் நாகன் ஸுமுகனைக் கண்டு மாதலி அவனைத் தன் மகளின் கணவனாகத் தேர்கிறான்.","ml":"വാസുകി ഭരിക്കുന്ന സർപ്പങ്ങളുടെ നഗരമായ ഭോഗവതി നാരദൻ മാതലിക്ക് കാണിക്കുന്നു; നിരവധി മഹാനാഗങ്ങളുടെ പേരുകളും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. ആര്യകന്റെ പൗത്രനായ സുന്ദരനായ യുവനാഗം സുമുഖനെ മാതലി കാണുന്നു; മകളുടെ ഭർത്താവായി അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.101; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इयं भोगवती नाम पुरी वासुकिपालिता ।\nयादृशी देवराजस्य पुरीवर्यामरावती ॥","meaning":{"en":"This city, Bhogavati, is ruled by Vasuki, and it is as splendid as Amaravati, the finest city of the king of the gods."}},{"n":2,"text":"एष शेषः स्थितो नागो येनेयं धार्यते सदा ।\nतपसा लोकमुख्येन प्रभावमहता मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here stands the serpent Shesha, by whom the earth is always held up, a being whose austerity and great power make him foremost in the world."}},{"n":3,"text":"श्वेतोच्चयनिभाकारो नानाविधविभूषणः ।\nसहस्रं धारयन्मूर्ध्नां ज्वालाजिह्वो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is shaped like a heap of white, adorned in many ways, bearing a thousand heads, tongues like flames, and great strength."}},{"n":4,"text":"इह नानाविधाकारा नानाविधविभूषणाः ।\nसुरसायाः सुता नागा निवसन्ति गतव्यथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here live without distress the Nagas, sons of Surasa, of many forms and many adornments."}},{"n":5,"text":"मणिस्वस्तिकचक्राङ्काः कमण्डलुकलक्षणाः ।\nसहस्रसंख्या बलिनः सर्वे रौद्राः स्वभावतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are marked with jewels, swastikas, wheels and water-pot signs; they number thousands, all mighty and fierce by nature."}},{"n":6,"text":"सहस्रशिरसः केचित्केचित्पञ्चशताननाः ।\nशतशीर्षास्तथा केचित्केचित्त्रिशिरसोऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some have a thousand heads, some five hundred faces, some a hundred heads, and some three heads."}},{"n":7,"text":"द्विपञ्चशिरसः केचित्केचित्सप्तमुखास्तथा ।\nमहाभोगा महाकायाः पर्वताभोगभोगिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some have ten heads, some seven mouths; they have huge hoods and huge bodies, coiling like mountains."}},{"n":8,"text":"बहूनीह सहस्राणि प्रयुतान्यर्बुदानि च ।\nनागानामेकवंशानां यथाश्रेष्ठांस्तु मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here there are many thousands, millions and tens of millions of Nagas of one lineage. Listen while I name the foremost of them."}},{"n":9,"text":"वासुकिस्तक्षकश्चैव कर्कोटकधनंजयौ ।\nकालीयो नहुषश्चैव कम्बलाश्वतरावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasuki, Takshaka, Karkotaka and Dhananjaya, Kaliya, Nahusha, and both Kambala and Ashvatara,"}},{"n":10,"text":"बाह्यकुण्डो मणिर्नागस्तथैवापूरणः खगः ।\nवामनश्चैलपत्रश्च कुकुरः कुकुणस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahyakunda, the serpent Mani, Apurana, Khaga, Vamana, Elapatra, Kukura and Kukuna,"}},{"n":11,"text":"आर्यको नन्दकश्चैव तथा कलशपोतकौ ।\nकैलासकः पिञ्जरको नागश्चैरावतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aryaka, Nandaka, Kalasha and Potaka, Kailasaka, Pinjaraka and the serpent Airavata,"}},{"n":12,"text":"सुमनोमुखो दधिमुखः शङ्खो नन्दोपनन्दकौ ।\nआप्तः कोटनकश्चैव शिखी निष्ठूरिकस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sumanomukha, Dadhimukha, Shankha, Nanda and Upananda, Apta, Kotanaka, Shikhi and Nishthurika,"}},{"n":13,"text":"तित्तिरिर्हस्तिभद्रश्च कुमुदो माल्यपिण्डकः ।\nद्वौ पद्मौ पुण्डरीकश्च पुष्पो मुद्गरपर्णकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tittiri, Hastibhadra, Kumuda, Malyapindaka, the two Padmas, Pundarika, Pushpa and Mudgaraparnaka,"}},{"n":14,"text":"करवीरः पीठरकः संवृत्तो वृत्त एव च ।\nपिण्डारो बिल्वपत्रश्च मूषिकादः शिरीषकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karavira, Pitharaka, Samvritta and Vritta, Pindara, Bilvapatra, Mushikada and Shirishaka,"}},{"n":15,"text":"दिलीपः शङ्खशीर्षश्च ज्योतिष्कोऽथापराजितः ।\nकौरव्यो धृतराष्ट्रश्च कुमारः कुशकस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dilipa, Shankhashirsha, Jyotishka and Aparajita, Kauravya, Dhritarashtra, Kumara and Kushaka,"}},{"n":16,"text":"विरजा धारणश्चैव सुबाहुर्मुखरो जयः ।\nबधिरान्धौ विकुण्डश्च विरसः सुरसस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Viraja, Dharana, Subahu, Mukhara, Jaya, Badhira, Andha, Vikunda, Virasa and Surasa."}},{"n":17,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवः कश्यपस्यात्मजाः स्मृताः ।\nमातले पश्य यद्यत्र कश्चित्ते रोचते वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and many others are remembered as sons of Kashyapa. Look, Matali, whether any one of them pleases you as groom."}},{"text":"कण्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kanva said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"मातलिस्त्वेकमव्यग्रः सततं संनिरीक्ष्य वै ।\nपप्रच्छ नारदं तत्र प्रीतिमानिव चाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matali, calm and steady, kept looking at one of them, and then asked Narada, seeming pleased."}},{"n":19,"text":"स्थितो य एष पुरतः कौरव्यस्यार्यकस्य च ।\nद्युतिमान्दर्शनीयश्च कस्यैष कुलनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Who is this radiant and handsome one standing in front of Kauravya and Aryaka? Whose family does this joy of his house belong to?"}},{"n":20,"text":"कः पिता जननी चास्य कतमस्यैष भोगिनः ।\nवंशस्य कस्यैष महान्केतुभूत इव स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who is his father, and who his mother? Of which serpent is he the son, and of which line is he the great banner, as it were?"}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रणिधानेन धैर्येण रूपेण वयसा च मे ।\nमनः प्रविष्टो देवर्षे गुणकेश्याः पतिर्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Divine sage, by his steadiness, his composure, his form and his age, he has entered my mind as the best husband for Gunakeshi.'"}},{"n":22,"text":"मातलिं प्रीतिमनसं दृष्ट्वा सुमुखदर्शनात् ।\nनिवेदयामास तदा माहात्म्यं जन्म कर्म च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Matali pleased at the sight of Sumukha, Narada then told him the youth's greatness, birth and deeds."}},{"n":23,"text":"ऐरावतकुले जातः सुमुखो नाम नागराट् ।\nआर्यकस्य मतः पौत्रो दौहित्रो वामनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"'This king of serpents named Sumukha was born in the line of Airavata. He is Aryaka's grandson, and the daughter's son of Vamana."}},{"n":24,"text":"एतस्य हि पिता नागश्चिकुरो नाम मातले ।\nनचिराद्वैनतेयेन पञ्चत्वमुपपादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His father, Matali, was the serpent named Chikura, whom Garuda not long ago brought to death.'"}},{"n":25,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीत्प्रीतमना मातलिर्नारदं वचः ।\nएष मे रुचितस्तात जामाता भुजगोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Matali, glad at heart, said to Narada, 'Sir, this best of serpents pleases me as a son-in-law."}},{"n":26,"text":"क्रियतामत्र यत्नो हि प्रीतिमानस्म्यनेन वै ।\nअस्य नागपतेर्दातुं प्रियां दुहितरं मुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Make an effort here, for I am delighted with him: let my dear daughter be given to this lord of serpents, sage.'"}}]}]}